# Prime OS — target-side packages for the desktop layer
#
# Derived from `pacman -Qe` on the reference desktop (Sean's CachyOS rig), 2026-09-27,
# filtered to what the product actually needs. Grouped by job, not alphabetically, so a
# change here is reviewable. Nothing is listed because it "looked useful".
#
# These install into the TARGET system (the installed machine), not the live ISO.

# --- session: compositor, lock, idle, wallpaper, portals ----------------------------
hyprland
hyprpaper
hypridle
hyprlock
xdg-desktop-portal-hyprland
xdg-desktop-portal-gtk
polkit-kde-agent
qt5-wayland
qt6-wayland

# --- the two bars + the launcher ----------------------------------------------------
waybar
rofi
wofi

# --- notifications, clipboard, screenshots, media keys ------------------------------
swaync
wl-clipboard
grim
slurp
playerctl

# --- login screen + a browser (no way to log in, or no browser, is not a desktop) ----
sddm
firefox

# --- terminals + file manager -------------------------------------------------------
kitty
alacritty
thunar
nemo
gvfs
xdg-user-dirs

# --- audio ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
pipewire
pipewire-pulse
pipewire-alsa
wireplumber
pavucontrol

# --- network, bluetooth, power -------------------------------------------------------
networkmanager
network-manager-applet
bluez
bluez-utils
power-profiles-daemon

# --- fonts + iconography (a bar with boxes instead of glyphs is a defect) ------------
noto-fonts
noto-fonts-cjk
noto-fonts-emoji
ttf-jetbrains-mono-nerd
ttf-meslo-nerd
ttf-dejavu
ttf-liberation
papirus-icon-theme

# --- snapshots, rollback, boot menu --------------------------------------------------
btrfs-progs
snapper
snap-pac
cachyos-snapper-support
efibootmgr
os-prober
plymouth
cachyos-plymouth-bootanimation

# --- the agent runtime + what the Prime layer is written in --------------------------
python
nodejs
npm
git
# checking that Prime updates are signed releases (ssh-keygen; the SSH server stays off)
openssh
wget
curl
uv

# --- day-to-day tools the workspace surfaces rely on ---------------------------------
btop
fastfetch
pacman-contrib
docker

# =====================================================================================
# NOT AVAILABLE FROM A REPO — these are AUR or third-party on the reference machine and
# cannot be installed during an image build. They need a local package repo or a
# first-boot step (neither exists yet). Listed so the gap is visible, not forgotten.
# =====================================================================================
# bibata-cursor-theme-bin        (AUR)  — cursor theme
# whitesur-gtk-theme             (AUR)  — GTK theme
# whitesur-icon-theme            (AUR)  — icon theme
# libastal-git / libastal-4-git  (AUR)  — the bar pills' GTK4 layer-shell bindings
# python-pywal / wallust               — wallpaper-driven theming
# google-chrome / discord / lmstudio-bin / orca-slicer-bin — Sean's own apps, not ours

# --- the Prime layer (layer/): what it needs beyond the above ------------------------
# Mirrors os/arch/packages.txt (the install-script path), so an ISO install and a
# CachyOS + install-script machine end up with the same desktop. tests/check-static.sh
# fails if the two drift apart.
adw-gtk-theme
base-devel
blueman
breeze-cursors
brightnessctl
cliphist
cmake
cpio
fd
flatpak
gnome-software
gnome-text-editor
gtk-layer-shell
gtk3
hyprpm
hyprpolkitagent
imagemagick
inter-font
jq
libnotify
meson
nwg-displays
pciutils
pkgconf
plocate
python-cairo
python-gobject
satty
uwsm
wl-clip-persist
xdg-utils

# --- added with the integrated layer (parity, updates & safety, packs) -------------
# everything os/arch/packages.txt lists, so a fresh install needs no download for Prime
arch-audit
btrfs-assistant
celluloid
cups
cups-filters
file-roller
gnome-calculator
gnome-keyring
gpu-screen-recorder
gtk4
gvfs-mtp
gvfs-smb
